hadiths[177]{hadithnumber,text}:
"115001","Yahya related to me from Malik that he had heard that a man said to Abdullah ibn Abbas"
"115002","Yahya related to me from Malik that he had heard that a man said to Abdullah ibn Abbas"
"115101","Yahya related to me from Malik that he had heard that a man came to Abdullah ibn Masud and said"
"115102","Yahya related to me from Malik that he had heard that a man came to Abdullah ibn Masud and said"
"115201","Yahya related to me from Malik from Yahya ibn Said from Abu Bakr ibn Hazm thatUmar ibn Abd al-Aziz had asked him what people said about the 'irrevocable' divorce"
"115202","Yahya related to me from Malik from Yahya ibn Said from Abu Bakr ibn Hazm thatUmar ibn Abd al-Aziz had asked him what people said about the 'irrevocable' divorce"
"115301","Yahya related to me from Malik from Ibn Shihab that Marwan ibn al-Hakam decided that if someone made three pronouncements of divorce"
"115302","Yahya related to me from Malik from Ibn Shihab that Marwan ibn al-Hakam decided that if someone made three pronouncements of divorce"
"115401","Yahya related to me from Malik that he had heard that Umar ibn al-Khattab had heard in a letter from Iraq that a man said to his wife"
"115402","Yahya related to me from Malik that he had heard that Umar ibn al-Khattab had heard in a letter from Iraq that a man said to his wife"
"115501","Yahya related to me from Malik that he had heard that Ali ibn Abi Talib used to say that if a man said to his wife"
"115502","Yahya related to me from Malik that he had heard that Ali ibn Abi Talib used to say that if a man said to his wife"
"115601","Yahya related to me from Malik from Nafi that Abdullah ibn Umar said that statements like \\""I cut myself off from you"""""""
"115602","Yahya related to me from Malik from Nafi that Abdullah ibn Umar said that statements like \\""I cut myself off from you"""""""
"115701","Yahya related to me from Malik from Yahya ibn Said from al-Qasim ibn Muhammad that a certain man had taken a slave-girl belonging to somebody else as a wife. He said to her people"
"115702","Yahya related to me from Malik from Yahya ibn Said from al-Qasim ibn Muhammad that a certain man had taken a slave-girl belonging to somebody else as a wife. He said to her people"
"115801","Malik related to me that it reached him that Umar ibn Abd al-Aziz wrote in his caliphate to some of his workers: ""Whatever the marriage guardian (al-munkah) stipulates — whether father or other — of a gift (hiba) or honor (karamah), it is for the woman if she seeks it."" Malik said: Regarding the woman whose father marries her off and stipulates in her dower the hiba by which he is honored: whatever condition the marriage contract is concluded upon is for his daughter if she seeks it. If her husband divorces her before consummation, the husband gets half of the hiba by which the marriage was concluded. Malik said: Regarding the man who marries off his minor son who has no wealth: the dower is upon his father if the boy had no wealth on the day he married. If the boy has wealth, the dower is from the boy's wealth, unless the father stipulates that the dower is upon him. That marriage is binding upon the son if he is minor and in his father's guardianship. Malik said: Regarding the man who divorces his wife before consummation while she is a virgin, and her father forgives half the dower: that is permissible for the husband from the father in what he has remitted. Malik said: That is because Allah, Blessed and Exalted, said in His Book: {Unless they forgive} (2:237) — they are the women who have been consummated with; {or he forgives in whose hand is the marriage knot} (2:237) — he is the father in his virgin daughter, and the master in his slave-girl. Malik said: This is what I have heard in that, and that is the matter upon us. Malik said: Regarding the Jewish or Christian woman under a Jewish or Christian husband who becomes Muslim before he consummates the marriage: she has no dower. Malik said: I do not see that a woman should be married for less than a quarter of a dinar, and that is the lowest amount in which the cutting (hadd for theft) becomes obligatory."
"115802","Yahya related to me from Malik that he heard Ibn Shihab say that if a man said to his wife"
"115901","Yahya related to me from Malik that he had heard that a man came to Abdullah ibn Umar"
"115902","Yahya related to me from Malik that he had heard that a man came to Abdullah ibn Umar"
"116001","Yahya related to me from Malik from Nafi that Abdullah ibn Umar said"
"116002","Yahya related to me from Malik from Ibn Shihab that Zayd ibn Thabit said, ""When a man takes his wife to his house and co-habits with her then the bride-price is obliged."""""""
"116101","Yahya related to me from Malik from Said ibn Sulayman ibn Zayd ibn Thabit that Kharija ibn Zayd ibn Thabit told him that he was sitting with Zayd ibn Thabit when Muhammad ibn Abi Atiq came to him with his eyes brimming with tears. Zayd asked him what the matter was. He said"
"116102","Yahya related to me from Malik from Said ibn Sulayman ibn Zayd ibn Thabit that Kharija ibn Zayd ibn Thabit told him that he was sitting with Zayd ibn Thabit when Muhammad ibn Abi Atiq came to him with his eyes brimming with tears. Zayd asked him what the matter was. He said"
"116201","Yahya related to me from Malik from Abd ar-Rahman ibn al-Qasim from his father that a man of Thaqif gave his wife command over herself"
"116202","Yahya related to me from Malik from Abd ar-Rahman ibn al-Qasim from his father that a man of Thaqif gave his wife command over herself"
"116301","Yahya related to me from Malik from Abd ar-Rahman ibn al-Qasim from his father that A'isha"
"116302","Yahya related to me from Malik from Abd ar-Rahman ibn al-Qasim from his father that A'isha"
"116401","Yahya related to me from Malik from Abd ar-Rahman ibn al-Qasim from his father that A'isha"
"116402","Yahya related to me from Malik from Abd ar-Rahman ibn al-Qasim from his father that A'isha"
"116501","Yahya related to me from Malik that he had heard that Abdullah ibn Umar and Abu Hurayra were asked about a man who gave his wife power over herself"
"116502","Yahya related to me from Malik that he had heard that Abdullah ibn Umar and Abu Hurayra were asked about a man who gave his wife power over herself"
"116601","Yahya related to me from Malik from Yahya ibn Said that Said ibn al-Musayyab said"
"116602","Yahya related to me from Malik from Yahya ibn Said that Said ibn al-Musayyab said"
"116701","Yahya related to me from Malik from Jafar ibn Muhammad from his father that Ali ibn Abi Talib said"
"116702","Yahya related to me from Malik from Jafar ibn Muhammad from his father that Ali ibn Abi Talib said"
"116801","Yahya related to me from Malik from Nafi that Abdullah ibn Umar said"
"116802","Yahya related to me from Malik from Nafi that Abdullah ibn Umar said"
"116901","Yahya related to me from Malik from Ibn Shihab that Said al-Musayyab and Abu Bakr ibn Abd ar-Rahman said about a man who made a vow to abstain from intercourse with his wife"
"116902","Yahya related to me from Malik from Ibn Shihab that Said al-Musayyab and Abu Bakr ibn Abd ar-Rahman said about a man who made a vow to abstain from intercourse with his wife"
"117001","Yahya related to me from Malik that he had heard that Marwan ibn al-Hakam decided about a man who had made a vow to abstain from intercourse with his wife"
"117002","Yahya related to me from Malik that he had heard that Marwan ibn al-Hakam decided about a man who had made a vow to abstain from intercourse with his wife"
"1171","[1171] Yahya told me, on the authority of Malik, that he had heard that Urwah ibn al-Zubayr used to say about the son of the cursed one, and he was born Adultery: If he dies, his mother inherits his rights according to the Book of God Almighty, and his brothers give his mother their rights, and he inherits The survivor is the slave of his mother, if she is your slave, and if she is an Arab, she inherits her rights, and his brothers inherit from his mother. Their rights, and what remained for the Muslims was a foothold in front of Malik Hadith: 1171 Arabic Hadith:"
"117201","Yahya related to me from Malik that he had asked Ibn Shihab about the ila of the slave. He said that it was like the ila of the free man"
"117202","Yahya related to me from Malik that he had asked Ibn Shihab about the ila of the slave. He said that it was like the ila of the free man"
"117301","Yahya related to me from Malik from Said ibn Amr ibn Sulaym az- Zuraqi that he asked al-Qasim ibn Muhammad about a man who made divorce conditional on his marrying a woman i.e. if he married her he would automatically divorce her. Al-Qasim ibn Muhammad said"
"117302","Yahya related to me from Malik from Said ibn Amr ibn Sulaym az- Zuraqi that he asked al-Qasim ibn Muhammad about a man who made divorce conditional on his marrying a woman i.e. if he married her he would automatically divorce her. Al-Qasim ibn Muhammad said"
"117401","Yahya related to me from Malik that he had heard that a man asked al-Qasim ibn Muhammad and Sulayman ibn Yasar about a man who pronounced dhihar from his wife before he had married her. They said"
"117402","Yahya related to me from Malik that he had heard that a man asked al-Qasim ibn Muhammad and Sulayman ibn Yasar about a man who pronounced dhihar from his wife before he had married her. They said"
"117501","Yahya related to me from Malik from Hisham ibn Urwa that his father said that a man who pronounced a dhihar from his four wives in one statement"
"117502","Yahya related to me from Malik from Hisham ibn Urwa that his father said that a man who pronounced a dhihar from his four wives in one statement"
"1176","[1176] Yahya told me, on the authority of Malik, on the authority of Ibn Shihab, on the authority of Talha ibn Abdullah ibn Awf - he said, and he was the most knowledgeable of them. Thus - on the authority of Abu Salama bin Abdul-Rahman bin Awf: that Abdul-Rahman bin Awf divorced his wife while he was ill. So Othman bin Affan inherited it from him, after her waiting period had expired. \\nMutta Imam Malik Hadith: 1176 Arabic Hadith:"
"117701","Yahya related to me from Malik from Hisham ibn Urwa that he heard a man ask Urwa ibn az-Zubayr about a man who said to his wife"
"117702","Yahya related to me from Malik from Hisham ibn Urwa that he heard a man ask Urwa ibn az-Zubayr about a man who said to his wife"
"117801","ahya related to me from Malik that he asked Ibn Shihab about the dhihar of a slave. He said"
"117802","ahya related to me from Malik that he asked Ibn Shihab about the dhihar of a slave. He said"
"117901","Yahya related to me from Malik from Rabia ibn Abi Abd ar-Rahman from al-Qasim ibn Muhammad that A'isha umm al-muminin"
"117902","Yahya related to me from Malik from Rabia ibn Abi Abd ar-Rahman from al-Qasim ibn Muhammad that A'isha umm al-muminin"
"118001","ahya related to me from Malik from Nafi that Abdullah ibn Umar said that a female slave who was the wife of a slave and then was set free"
"118002","ahya related to me from Malik from Nafi that Abdullah ibn Umar said that a female slave who was the wife of a slave and then was set free"
"118101","Yahya related to me from Malik from Ibn Shihab from Urwa ibn az- Zubayr that a mawla of the tribe of Banu Adi called Zabra told him that she had been the wife of a slave when she was a slave-girl. Then she was set free and she sent a message to Hafsa"
"118102","Yahya related to me from Malik from Ibn Shihab from Urwa ibn az- Zubayr that a mawla of the tribe of Banu Adi called Zabra told him that she had been the wife of a slave when she was a slave-girl. Then she was set free and she sent a message to Hafsa"
"118201","Yahya related to me from Malik that he had heard that Said ibn al-Musayyab said that if a man married a woman"
"118202","Yahya related to me from Malik that he had heard that Said ibn al-Musayyab said that if a man married a woman"
"118301","And it was narrated to me from Malik, from Ibn Shihab, from Qabisa ibn Dhu'ayb, that a man asked Uthman ibn Affan about two sisters who are owned as slaves, whether they could be joined together. Uthman said: \A verse has made them lawful"
"118302","And it was narrated to me from Malik, from Ibn Shihab, that he said: \Every divorced woman is entitled to a mut'ah (consolatory gift).\"""""""""
"118401","Yahya related. to me from Malik from Yahya ibn Said that Amra bint Abd ar-Rahman told him from Habiba bint Sahl al-Ansari that she had been the wife of Thabit ibn Qays ibn Shammas. The Messenger of Allah"
"118402","Yahya related. to me from Malik from Yahya ibn Said that Amra bint Abd ar-Rahman told him from Habiba bint Sahl al-Ansari that she had been the wife of Thabit ibn Qays ibn Shammas. The Messenger of Allah"
"118501","Yahya related to me from Malik from Nafi from a mawla of Safiyya bint Abi Ubayd that she gave all that she possessed to her husband as compensation for her divorce from him"
"118502","Yahya related to me from Malik from Nafi from a mawla of Safiyya bint Abi Ubayd that she gave all that she possessed to her husband as compensation for her divorce from him"
"118601","Yahya related to me from Malik from Nafi that Rubayyi bint Muawwidh ibn Afra came with her paternal uncle to Abdullah ibn Umar and told him that she had divorced her husband for a compensation in the time of Uthman ibn Affan"
"118602","Yahya related to me from Malik from Nafi that Rubayyi bint Muawwidh ibn Afra came with her paternal uncle to Abdullah ibn Umar and told him that she had divorced her husband for a compensation in the time of Uthman ibn Affan"
"118701","Yahya related to me from Malik that he had heard that Said ibn al-Musayyab and Sulayman ibn Yasar and Ibn Shihab all said that a woman who divorced for a compensation had the same idda as a divorced woman - three periods. Malik said that a woman who ransomed herself could not return to her husband except by a new marriage. If someone married her and then separated from her before he had intercourse with her"
"118702","Yahya related to me from Malik that he had heard that Said ibn al-Musayyab and Sulayman ibn Yasar and Ibn Shihab all said that a woman who divorced for a compensation had the same idda as a divorced woman - three periods. Malik said that a woman who ransomed herself could not return to her husband except by a new marriage. If someone married her and then separated from her before he had intercourse with her"
"118801","Yahya related to me from Malik from Ibn Shihab that Sahl ibn Sad as-Saidi told him that Uwaymir al-Ajlani came to Asim ibn Adi al- Ansari and said to him"
"118802","Yahya related to me from Malik from Ibn Shihab that Sahl ibn Sad as-Saidi told him that Uwaymir al-Ajlani came to Asim ibn Adi al- Ansari and said to him"
"118901","Yahya related to me from Malik from Nafic from Abdullah ibn Umar that a man cursed his wife in the time of the Messenger of Allah"
"118902","Yahya related to me from Malik from Nafic from Abdullah ibn Umar that a man cursed his wife in the time of the Messenger of Allah"
"119001","Yahya related to me from Malik that he had heard that `Urwa ibn az-Zubayr said that if the child of the woman against whom li`an had been pronounced or the child of fornication"
"119002","Yahya related to me from Malik that he had heard that `Urwa ibn az-Zubayr said that if the child of the woman against whom li`an had been pronounced or the child of fornication"
"1191","[1191] Yahya narrated to me, on the authority of Malik, on the authority of Nafi’: that Abdullah bin Umar divorced his wife while she was menstruating, according to a covenant. The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, so Omar ibn al-Khattab asked the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, about that, and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: He ordered it, so let him review it. Then He may keep her until she is pure, then she will menstruate, then become pure, then if he wishes he may keep her after that, and if he wishes he may divorce her before he touches her, so he may The waiting period for which God has commanded women to be divorced - Muwatta Imam Malik Hadith: 1191 Arabic Hadith:"
"119201","Yahya related to me from Malik from Ibn Shihab from Muhammad ibn Abd ar-Rahman ibn Thawban that Muhammad ibn Iyas ibn al-Bukayr said"
"119202","Yahya related to me from Malik from Ibn Shihab from Muhammad ibn Abd ar-Rahman ibn Thawban that Muhammad ibn Iyas ibn al-Bukayr said"
"119301","Yahya related to me from Malik from Yahya ibn Said from Bukayr ibn Abdullah al-Ashajj from an-Numan ibn Abi Ayyash al Ansari from Ata ibn Yasar that a man came and asked Abdullah ibn Amr ibn al-As about a man who divorced his wife three times before he had had intercourse with her Ata said"
"119302","Yahya related to me from Malik from Yahya ibn Said from Bukayr ibn Abdullah al-Ashajj from an-Numan ibn Abi Ayyash al Ansari from Ata ibn Yasar that a man came and asked Abdullah ibn Amr ibn al-As about a man who divorced his wife three times before he had had intercourse with her Ata said"
"119401","Yahya related to me from Malik from Yahya ibn Said that Bukayr ibn Abdullah al-Ashajj informed him that Muawiya ibn Abi Ayyash al- Ansari told him that he was sitting with Abdullah ibn az-Zubayr and Asim ibn Umar ibn al-Khattab when Muhammad ibn Iyas ibn al-Bukayr came up to them and said"
"119402","Yahya related to me from Malik from Yahya ibn Said that Bukayr ibn Abdullah al-Ashajj informed him that Muawiya ibn Abi Ayyash al- Ansari told him that he was sitting with Abdullah ibn az-Zubayr and Asim ibn Umar ibn al-Khattab when Muhammad ibn Iyas ibn al-Bukayr came up to them and said"
"119501","Malik related to me from Ibn Shihab that it reached him that women were in the time of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ who embraced Islam in their lands without migrating, while their husbands, when they embraced Islam, were disbelievers. Among them was the daughter of al-Walid ibn al-Mughirah. She was under Safwan ibn Umayyah. She embraced Islam on the Day of the Conquest (of Makkah), and her husband Safwan ibn Umayyah fled from Islam. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ sent to him his paternal cousin Wahb ibn Umayr with the cloak of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ as a guarantee of safety (aman) for Safwan ibn Umayyah. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ called him to Islam and to come to him: ""If you are pleased with a matter, accept it; otherwise, I will grant you respite for two months."" When Safwan came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ with his cloak, he called out to him before the people: ""O Muhammad! This Wahb ibn Umayr came to me with your cloak and claimed that you called me to come to you: if I am pleased with a matter, I accept it; otherwise, you will grant me respite for two months."" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: ""Dismount, Abu Wahb."" He said: ""No, by Allah, I will not dismount until you make it clear to me."" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: ""Rather, you have respite for four months."" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ went out towards Hawazin at Hunayn. He sent to Safwan ibn Umayyah asking to borrow equipment and weapons he had. Safwan said: ""Willingly or unwillingly?"" He said: ""Rather, willingly."" So he lent him the equipment and weapons he had. Then Safwan went out with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ while he was a disbeliever. He witnessed Hunayn and al-Ta'if while a disbeliever, and his wife was Muslim. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ did not separate between him and his wife until Safwan embraced Islam, and his wife remained with him by that marriage."
"119502","Yahya related to me from Malik from Ibn Shihab that Talha ibn Abdullah ibn Awf said"
"119601","Yahya related to me from Malik from Abdullah ibn al-Fadl from al- Araj that Uthman ibn Affan made the wives of ibn Mukmil inherit from him"
"119602","Yahya related to me from Malik from Abdullah ibn al-Fadl from al- Araj that Uthman ibn Affan made the wives of ibn Mukmil inherit from him"
"119701","And from Malik from Ibn Shihab that Umm Hakim bint al-Harith ibn Hisham, who was married to Ikrimah ibn Abi Jahl, accepted Islam on the day of the Conquest, and her husband Ikrimah ibn Abi Jahl fled from Islam until he arrived in Yemen. Umm Hakim then traveled until she came to him in Yemen and called him to"
"119702","Yahya related to me from Malik that he heard Rabia ibn Abi Abd ar-Rahman say"
"119801","Yahya related to me from Malik from Yahya ibn Said that Muhammad ibn Yahya ibn Habban said"
"119802","Yahya related to me from Malik from Yahya ibn Said that Muhammad ibn Yahya ibn Habban said"
"119901","Yahya related to me from Malik that he had heard Ibn Shihab say"
"119902","Yahya related to me from Malik that he had heard Ibn Shihab say"
"120001","Yahya related to me from Malik that he had heard that Abd ar- Rahman ibn Awf divorced his wife"
"120002","Yahya related to me from Malik that he had heard that Abd ar- Rahman ibn Awf divorced his wife"
"120101","Yahya related to me from Malik from Nafi that Abdullah ibn Umar said"
"120102","Yahya related to me from Malik from Ibr. Shihab from al-Araj that Abu Hurayra said, ""The worst food is the food of a wedding feast to which the rich are invited and the poor are left out. If anyone rejects an invitation, he has rebelled against Allah and His Messenger."""""""
"120201","Yahya related to me from Malik that Ishaq ibn Abdullah ibn Abi Talha heard Anas ibn Malik say that a certain tailor invited the Messenger of Allah, may Allah bless him and grant him peace, to eat some food which he had prepared. Anas said, ""I went with the Messenger of Allah, may Allah bless him and grant him peace, to eat the food. He served barley bread and a soup with pumpkin in it. I saw the Messenger of Allah, may Allah bless him and grant him peace, going after the pumpkin around the dish, so I have always liked pumpkin since that day."""""""
"120202","Yahya related to me from Malik that Ibn Shihab said"
"1203","[1203] And he told me on the authority of Malik, on the authority of Nafi’: that Abdullah ibn Umar divorced his wife in the residence of Hafsa, the wife of the Prophet. May God’s prayers and peace be upon him, and he was on his way to the mosque, so he used to take the other route from the backs of the houses, as he did not want to He asks her permission until he comes back to her. \\nMutta Imam Malik Hadith: 1203 Arabic Hadith:"
"120401","Yahya related to me from Malik from Abu'z-Zinad from Sulayman ibn Yasar that Nufay"
"120402","Yahya related to me from Malik from Abu'z-Zinad from Sulayman ibn Yasar that Nufay"
"120501","Yahya related to me from Malik from Ibn Shihab from Said ibn al- Musayyab that Nufay"
"120502","Yahya related to me from Malik from Ibn Shihab from Said ibn al- Musayyab that Nufay"
"120601","Yahya related to me from Malik from Abdu Rabbih ibn Said from Muhammad ibn Ibrahim ibn al-Harith at-Taymi that Nufay"
"120602","Yahya related to me from Malik from Abdu Rabbih ibn Said from Muhammad ibn Ibrahim ibn al-Harith at-Taymi that Nufay"
"120701","Yahya related to me from Malik from Nafi that Abdullah ibn Umar said"
"120702","Yahya related to me from Malik from Nafi that Abdullah ibn Umar said"
"120801","Yahya related to me from Malik from Ibn Shihab that Rafi ibn Khadij married the daughter of Muhammad ibn Maslama al-Ansari. She was with him until she grew older, and then he married a young girl and preferred the young girl to her. She begged him to divorce her, so he divorced her and then he gave her time until she had almost finished her idda period and then he returned and still preferred the young girl. She therefore asked him to divorce her. He divorced her once, and then returned to her, and still preferred the young girl, and she asked him to divorce her. He said, ""What do you want? There is only one divorce left. If you like, continue and put up with what you see of preference, and if you like, I will separate from you."" She said, ""I will continue in spite of the preference."" He kept her in spite of that. Rafi did not see that he had done any wrong action when she remained with him in spite of preference."""""
"120802","Yahya related to me from Malik from Nafi that Abdullah ibn Umar said"
"1209","Malik said, ""Neither a free man nor a slave who divorces a slave- girl nor a slave who divorces a free woman, in an irrevocable divorce, is obliged to pay maintenance even if she is pregnant, and he cannot return to her."" Malik said, ""A free man is not obliged to pay for the suckling of his son when he is a slave of other people, nor is a slave obliged to spend his money for what his master owns except with the permission of his master"
"1210","Yahya related to me from Malik from Yahya ibn Said from Said ibn al-Musayyab that Umar ibn al-Khattab said"
"1211","Yahya related to me from Malik from Nafi that Abdullah ibn Umar divorced his wife while she was menstruating in the time of the Messenger of Allah"
"1212","Yahya related to me from Malik from Ibn Shihab from Urwa ibn az- Zubayr from A'isha"
"1213","Yahya related to me from Malik that Ibn Shihab said that he heard Abu Bakr ibn Abd ar-Rahman say"
"1214","Yahya related to me from Malik from Nafi and Zayd ibn Aslam from Sulayman ibn Yasar that al-Ahwas died in Syria when his wife had begun her third menstrual period after he had divorced her. Muawiya ibn Abi Sufyan wrote and asked Zayd ibn Thabit about that. Zayd wrote to him"
"1215","Yahya related to me from Malik that he had heard that Abu Bakr ibn Abd ar-Rahman and Sulayman ibn Yasar and Ibn Shihab used to say"
"1216","Yahya related to me from Malik from Nafi that Abdullah ibn Umar said"
"1217","Yahya related to me from Malik from al-Fudayl ibn Abi Abdullah, the mawla of al-Mahri that al-Qasim ibn Muhammad and Salim ibn Abdullah said, ""When a woman is divorced and begins her third period, she is clearly separated from him and is free to marry again"
"1218","Yahya related to me from Malik that he had heard that Said ibn al-Musayyab and Ibn Shihab and Sulayman ibn Yasar all said"
"1219","Yahya related to me from Malik that he heard Ibn Shihab say, ""The idda of the divorced woman is reckoned by the menstrual cycles even if she is estranged ."" (The reason the idda is normally reckoned by the menstrual cycle is to see whether the woman is pregnant or not)"
"1220","Yahya related to me from Malik from Yahya ibn Said from a man of the Ansar that his wife asked him for a divorce"
"1221","Yahya related to me from Malik thal Yahya ibn Said heard al-Qasim ibn Muhammad and Sulayman ibn Yasar both mention that Yahya ibn Said ibn al-As divorced the daughter of Abd ar-Rahman ibn al-Hakam irrevocably"
"1222","Yahya related to me from Malik from Nafi that the daughter of Said ibn Zayd ibn Amr ibn Nufayl was the wife of Abdullah ibn Umar ibn Uthman ibn Affan"
"1223","Yahya related to me from Malik from Nafi that Abdullah ibn Umar divorced one of his wives in the house of Hafsa"
"1224","Yahya related to me from Malik from Yahya ibn Said that Said ibn al-Musayyab was asked who was obliged to pay the rent for a woman whose husband divorced her while she was in a leased house. Said ibn al-Musayyab said"
"1225","Yahya related to me from Malik from Abdullah ibn Yazid"
"1226","Yahya related to me from Malik that he heard Ibn Shihab say, ""The woman who is absolutely divorced does not leave her house until she is free to remarry. She has no maintenance unless she is pregnant. In that circumstance the husband spends on her until she gives birth."" Malik said, ""This is what is done among us"
"1227","Malik said, ""What is done among us when a slave divorces a slave- girl when she is a slave and then she is set free, is that her idda is the idda of a slave-girl, and her being set free does not change her idda whether or not he can still return to her. Her idda is not altered."" Malik added, ""The hadd-punishment which a slave incurs is the same as this. When he is freed after he has incurred but before the punishment has been executed, his hadd is the hadd of the slave."" Malik said, ""When a free man divorces a slave-girl three times, her idda is two periods. When a slave divorces a free woman twice, her idda is three periods."" Malik said about a man who had a slave-girl as a wife, and he bought her and set her free, ''Her idda is the idda of a slave-girl, i.e. two periods, as long as he has not had intercourse with her. If he has had intercourse with her after buying her and before he set her free, she only has to wait until one period has passed . "" Yahya related to me from Malik from Yahya ibn Said and from Yazid ibn Abdullah ibn Qusayt al-Laythi that Said ibn al-Musayyab said, ''Umar ibn al-Khattab said, 'If a woman is divorced and has one or two periods and then stops menstruating, she must wait nine months. If it is clear that she is pregnant, that is that. If not, she must do an idda of three months after the nine, and then she is free to marry"
"1228","Yahya related to me from Malik from Yahya ibn Said that Said ibn al-Musayyab said"
"1229","Yahya related to me from Malik from Ibn Shihab that Said ibn al- Musayyab said"
"1230","Yahya related to me from Malik that he had heard that Ali ibn Abi Talib said about the two arbiters about whom Allah"
"1231","Yahya related to me from Malik that he had heard that Umar ibn al-Khattab"
"1232","Yahya related to me from Malik that he had heard that Abdullah ibn Masud said that there was nothing binding on someone who said"
"1233","Yahya related to me from Malik from Ibn Shihab that Said ibn al- Musayyab said"
"1234","Yahya related to me from Malik that he had asked Ibn Shihab about whether the deadline was set from the day he had married her"
"1235","Yahya related to me from Malik that Ibn Shihab said"
"1236","Yahya related to me from Malik that Ibn Shihab said that he had heard Said ibn al-Musayyab"
"1237","Yahya related to me from Malik from Thabit ibn al-Ahnaf that he married an umm walad of Abd ar-Rahman ibn Zayd ibn al-Khattab. He said"
"1238","Yahya related to me from Malik that Abdullah ibn Dinar said"
"1239","Yahya related to me from Malik from Hisham ibn Urwa that his father said"
"1240","Yahya related to me from Malik from Thawr ibn Zayd ad-Dili that Allah"
"1241","Yahya related to me from Malik that he had heard that Said ibn al-Musayyab and Sulayman ibn Yasar were asked about a man who divorced when he was drunk. They said"
"1242","Yahya related to me from Malik that he had heard that Said ibn al-Musayyab said"
"1243","Yahya related to me from Malik from Abdu Rabbih ibn Said ibn Qays that Abu Salama ibn Abd ar-Rahman said that Abdullah ibn Abbas and Abu Hurayra were asked when a pregnant woman whose husband had died could remarry. Ibn Abbas said"
"1244","Yahya related to me from Malik from Nafi that Abdullah ibn Umar was asked about a woman whose husband died while she was pregnant"
"1245","Yahya related to me from Malik from Hisham ibn 'Urwa from his father that al-Miswar ibn Makhrama told him that Subaya al-Aslamiya gave birth a few nights after the death of her husband. The Messenger of Allah"
"1246","Yahya related to me from Malik from Yahya ibn Said from Sulayman ibn Yasar that Abdullah ibn Abbas and Abu Salama ibn Abd ar-Rahman ibn Awf differed on the question of a wornan who gave birth a few nights after the death of her husband. Abu Salama said"
"1247","Yahya related to me from Malik from Said ibn Ishaq ibn Kab ibn Ujra from his paternal aunt"
"1248","Yahya related to me from Malik from Humayd ibn Qays al-Makki from Amr ibn Shuayb from Said ibn al-Musayyab that Umar ibn al-Khattab sent back widows from the desert and prevented them from doing the hajj"
"1249","Yahya related to me from Malik from Yahya ibn Saqd that he had heard that as-Sa'ib ibn Khabbab died"
"1250","Yahya related to me from Malik that Hisham ibn Urwa said about a Bedouin woman whose husband died"
"1251","Yahya related to me from Malik from Nafi that Abdullan ibn Umar said, ""The only place a woman whose husband has died and a woman who is absolutely divorced can spend the night is in their houses"
"1252","Yahya related to me from Malik that Yahya ibn Said said that he had heard al-Qasim ibn Muhammad say that Zayd ibn Abd al-Malik separated some men and their wives who were slave-girls who had borne children to men who had died"
"1253","Malik related to me from Nafi that Abdullah ibn Umar said"
"1254","Malik said, ""This is what is done among us."" Malik added, ""If she does not have a menstrual period, her idda is three months"
"1255","Yahya related to me from Malik that he had heard that Said ibn al-Musayyab and Sulayman ibn Yasar said"
"1256","Yahya related to me the like of that from Malik from Ibn Shihab. Malik said"
"1257","Yahya related to me from Malik from Rabia ibn Abi Abd ar-Rahman from Muhammad ibn Yahya ibn Habban that Ibn Muhayriz said"
"1258","And it was narrated to me from Malik, from Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Qasim, from his father, that he informed him: \Aisha"
"1259","And it was narrated to me from Malik, from Ibrahim ibn Uqbah, that he asked Sa'id ibn al-Musayyab about suckling. Sa'id said: \Anything that occurs within two years"
"1260","Yahya related to me from Malik from Nafi that Abdullah ibn Umar did not practise coitus interruptus and thought that it was disapproved"
"1261","Yahya related to me from Malik from Damra ibn Said al-Mazini from al-Hajjaj ibn Amr ibn Ghaziya that he was sitting with Zayd ibn Thabit when Ibn Fahd came to him. He was from the Yemen. He said"
"1262","Yahya related to me from Malik from Humayd ibn Qays al-Makki that a man called Dhafif said that Ibn Abbas was asked about coitus interruptus. He called a slave-girl of his and said"
"1263","Yahya related to me from Malik from Abdullah ibn Abi Bakr ibn Muhammad ibn Amr ibn Hazm from Humayd ibn Nafi that Zaynab bint Abi Salama related these three traditions to him. Zaynab said"
"1264","Zaynab said, ""I went to the house of Zaynab bint Jahsh, the wife of the Prophet, may Allah bless him and grant him peace, when her brother had died. She called for perfume and put some on and said, 'By Allah! I have no need of perfume, but I heard the Messenger of Allah, may Allah bless him and grant him peace, say, 'It is not halal for a woman who trusts in Allah and the Last Day to abstain from adornment in mourning for someone who has died for more than three nights, except for four months and ten days for a husband"
"1265","Zaynab said, ""I heard my mother, Umm Salama, the wife of the Prophet, may Allah bless him and grant him peace, say that a woman came to the Messenger of Allah, may Allah bless him and grant him peace, and said, 'Messenger of Allah! My daughter's husband died, and her eyes are troubling her, can she put kohl on them?' The Messenger of Allah, may Allah bless him and grant him peace, said, 'No' two or three times. Then he said, 'It is only four months and ten days. In the Jahiliyya, none of you threw away the piece of dung until a year had passed.' "" Humayd ibn Nafi said, ""I asked Zaynab to explain what 'throwing away the piece of dung at the end of a year' meant. Zaynab said, 'In the Jahiliyya when a woman's husband died, she went into a small tent and dressed in the worst of clothes. She did not touch perfume or anything until a year had passed. Then she was brought an animal - a donkey, a sheep, or a bird, and she would break her idda with it, by rubbing her body against it (taftaddu). Rarely did she break her idda with anything (by rubbing herself against it) but that it died. Then she would come out and would be given a piece of dung. She would throw it away and then return to whatever she wished of perfumes or whatever.' "" Malik explained, 'Taftaddu' means to wipe her skin with it in the same way as with a healing charm"
"1266","Yahya related to me from Malik from Nafi from Safiyya bint Abi Ubayd from A'isha and Hafsa"
"1267","Yahya related to me from Malik that he had heard that Umm Salama"
"1268","Yahya related to me from Malik that he had heard that Salim ibn Abdullah and Sulayman ibn Yasar said that if a woman whose husband had died feared that an inflammation of her eyes might affect her sight or that some complaint might befall her"
"1269","Yahya related to me from Malik from Nafic that Saffiyya bint Abi Ubayd suffered from an eye-complaint while she was in mourning for her husband"
"1270","Yahya related to me from Malik that he had heard that the Messenger of Allah"
"1271","Yahya related to me from Malik that he had heard that Umm Salama"
